{"page_content": "Step 6: Document the analogue approach\n\nIf the read-across is considered to be suitable, the approach should be documented according to an appropriate format in order to justify that the approach may be used instead of testing (see Section R.6.2.6). The justification for the read-across should include an explanation of the rationale, as well as the assessment including all relevant supporting information. Ideally examples of unsuitable read-across should also be documented.\n\nTable R. 6-2 Selected internet-based tools for analogue-searching", "metadata": {"doc_id": "11e32357-c9fe-4e86-952b-c861f93a7dcd", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "information_requirements_r6_en.pdf"}}